    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A vanity case is a box made to hold grooming and cosmetic essentials. The oldest known example was unearthed by British archaeologist Howard Carter and dates back more than 3,000 years. In China, the dressing case known as lian evolved from the Warring States period through the Ming and Qing dynasties; in the Warring States and Qin-Han eras these were often lacquered, and reserved for the nobility.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "text": null,
      "url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/kku4c9k/38fe225f9741b5fe.jpg",
      "full_url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/kku4c9k/38fe225f9741b5fe.jpg",
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Europe took the vanity case to new heights in the 1920s, when leading jewelers crafted them from precious materials with virtuoso techniques — enamel painting, gemstone inlay and more — often finishing the top with a wrist chain or handle so the case could travel to balls, dinners and beyond.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "grid",
      "text": null,
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": [
        {
          "url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/kku4c9k/cece5b51b8c44044.jpg",
          "full_url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/kku4c9k/cece5b51b8c44044.jpg",
          "price": ""
        },
        {
          "url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/kku4c9k/426d44e8c02ed9c9.jpg",
          "full_url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/kku4c9k/426d44e8c02ed9c9.jpg",
          "price": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "caption",
      "text": "Left: vanity case set with enamel, chalcedony, coral, diamonds and jade beads, by Mauboussin, 1920s. Right: engraved gold vanity case set with rubies, by Boucheron, circa 1950s",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The Cube borrows from the handheld vanity case, pairing a small boxy shape with a horizontal metal frame and a sliding top strap. The monogram canvas gives the silhouette a soft structure, lending this classic vanity inspiration an easy, languid French attitude.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
